{"id": "en_story_kodak", "tag": "BUSINESS FAILS", "cta": "MORE TRUE STORIES LIKE THIS", "ctaSmall": "follow", "ctaWhere": "new story every day", "accent": "#FFC83D", "lang": "en", "total": 78.41, "segments": [{"text": "Imagine inventing the exact technology that ultimately destroys your entire multi billion dollar business empire.", "start": 0.0, "end": 5.56}, {"text": "In 1975 a brilliant Kodak engineer named Steve Sasson builds the first digital camera.", "start": 6.02, "end": 11.34}, {"text": "This revolutionary machine is massive and awkward, roughly the exact physical size of a kitchen toaster.", "start": 11.96, "end": 16.8}, {"text": "The experimental device captures tiny black and white images at a mere 0.01 megapixels.", "start": 17.26, "end": 22.26}, {"text": "Waiting for the camera to process a single picture takes roughly 23 agonizing seconds of time.", "start": 22.84, "end": 27.32}, {"text": "The image data saves slowly onto a standard audio cassette tape hidden inside the device.", "start": 27.32, "end": 32.36}, {"text": "Instead of celebrating this futuristic breakthrough, terrified company management looks at the prototype with pure dread.", "start": 33.14, "end": 39.12}, {"text": "The powerful executives quickly realize this new digital invention will destroy their extremely lucrative film business.", "start": 39.88, "end": 45.24}, {"text": "They decide to bury the threatening technology and focus entirely on selling traditional photographic film.", "start": 45.9, "end": 50.56}, {"text": "Decades pass quietly while the rest of the world slowly wakes up to digital photography.", "start": 51.16, "end": 54.86}, {"text": "The unstoppable rise of digital cameras completely obliterates traditional film sales across the global market.", "start": 54.86, "end": 60.84}, {"text": "Without enough time to adapt to the modern era, the once mighty company collapses.", "start": 61.46, "end": 65.12}, {"text": "In January 2012, Kodak officially files for bankruptcy after failing to survive the digital revolution.", "start": 65.98, "end": 71.5}, {"text": "Would you have buried the camera to save your business or released it immediately?", "start": 72.18, "end": 75.26}], "words": [["Imagine", 0.0, 0.56], ["inventing", 0.56, 1.32], ["the", 1.32, 1.4], ["exact", 1.4, 1.66], ["technology", 1.66, 2.18], ["that", 2.18, 2.34], ["ultimately", 2.34, 2.76], ["destroys", 2.76, 3.18], ["your", 3.18, 3.5], ["entire", 3.5, 3.92], ["multi", 3.92, 4.26], ["billion", 4.26, 4.66], ["dollar", 4.66, 4.92], ["business", 4.92, 5.18], ["empire.", 5.18, 5.56], ["In", 6.02, 6.36], ["1975", 6.36, 7.02], ["a", 7.4, 7.48], ["brilliant", 7.48, 7.86], ["Kodak", 7.86, 8.28], ["engineer", 8.28, 8.64], ["named", 8.64, 8.92], ["Steve", 8.92, 9.3], ["Sasson", 8.93, 9.086], ["builds", 9.66, 10.08], ["the", 10.08, 10.32], ["first", 10.32, 10.56], ["digital", 10.56, 11.0], ["camera.", 11.0, 11.34], ["This", 11.96, 12.22], ["revolutionary", 12.22, 12.58], ["machine", 12.58, 13.02], ["is", 13.02, 13.24], ["massive", 13.24, 13.7], ["and", 13.7, 13.98], ["awkward,", 13.98, 14.3], ["roughly", 14.68, 14.88], ["the", 14.88, 15.1], ["exact", 15.1, 15.36], ["physical", 15.36, 15.76], ["size", 15.76, 16.0], ["of", 16.0, 16.2], ["a", 16.2, 16.28], ["kitchen", 16.28, 16.42], ["toaster.", 16.42, 16.8], ["The", 17.26, 17.58], ["experimental", 17.58, 17.88], ["device", 17.88, 18.26], ["captures", 18.26, 18.7], ["tiny", 18.7, 19.1], ["black", 19.1, 19.44], ["and", 19.44, 19.58], ["white", 19.58, 19.74], ["images", 19.74, 20.04], ["at", 20.04, 20.46], ["a", 20.46, 20.52], ["mere", 20.52, 20.68], ["0.01", 20.53, 20.65], ["megapixels.", 21.44, 22.26], ["Waiting", 22.84, 23.1], ["for", 23.1, 23.24], ["the", 23.24, 23.32], ["camera", 23.32, 23.48], ["to", 23.48, 23.6], ["process", 23.6, 23.92], ["a", 23.92, 24.14], ["single", 24.14, 24.42], ["picture", 24.42, 24.74], ["takes", 24.74, 25.14], ["roughly", 25.14, 25.44], ["23", 25.44, 26.04], ["agonizing", 26.04, 26.66], ["seconds", 26.66, 